	<Uses />
</Figure>

## How we think

<Figure n={3} caption="Five ideas, each drawn with the real system: the devices a model runs on, the first run's recommendation, the three places the character lives, a control on its grid and one token chain.">
	<Principles />
</Figure>

## How it fits together

<Figure n={4} caption="The products and their repositories. llama-brand supplies the brand; llama.cpp holds the engine, Llama UI in ui/lib/ui and Llama Chat in ui/apps/chat, this Storybook's home; the native apps run llama-server and open Llama Chat. llama.app shows models the way Llama Chat does.">
	<Products />
</Figure>

Inside Llama UI, the tokens go from primitives to semantic roles to components, in `ui/lib/ui/src/lib/styles/tokens/`, and `DESIGN.md` is generated from them. Llama UI draws the interface and handles interaction; each app owns its own state.

